-- title:
--   Tower family of coarse points over connected Noetherian bases
-- statement:
--   The theorem produces, for the whole Hecke tower away from $r$ and $\bar r$, a system of $B$-points of the coarse moduli schemes $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over connected Noetherian bases, characterised on rigidified curves. Its hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`), and a nonzero natural number $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (`hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`).
--
--   **Coefficient rings** (`hdvr`–`K₀`, `Onr`–`hFr`, `vdet`, `hvdet`). $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$ is irreducible, $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal; every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$. Finally $\mathrm{vdet}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (multiplicatively written) is a homomorphism with $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion side.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ the completion is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies above $r$ or above $\bar r$; $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it (`hΛ`), and `hΛℤ` asserts that every integer lies in $\Lambda$.
--
--   **Moduli data over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$.** A scheme $\mathcal X$ with structure morphism $f$ and a point assignment `pt` on fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, such that `h𝒳` holds: isomorphism invariance, compatibility with pull-back along ring maps, bijectivity of `pt` on points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property of a coarse moduli space. An auxiliary level $n\ge 3$ prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$ (`hn`, `hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`), a scheme $M$ with `ptF` and `hM : IsFineModuli Λ N n M fM ptF`, a group $G$ acting on $M$ through $\rho$ with labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ and `hρ : IsLevelTwistAction` (action over the base, twisting of full level structures, and the labelling clauses modulo $n$), and a forgetful morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hp`) which is $G$-invariant (`hρp`) and carries `ptF` to `pt` (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **The tower and the Atkin–Lehner maps.** For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point assignment `ptT ℓ` on pairs (curve, extra level-$\ell$ structure) and `h𝒴 ℓ : IsCoarseModuliT` (the same five clauses for such pairs), together with degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) such that $d_0$ forgets the extra level (`hd₀`) and $d_1$ sends the point of $(E,C)$ to the point of any curve level-$\ell$-isogenous to it (`hd₁`); and endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and the completion of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ at a finite place is a division algebra exactly at $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ with $R_1\le\Lambda_1$, a finite-idelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ with `hS₁` asserting that $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$, an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0\colon\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$, and the prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ above $r$.
--
--   **The arithmetic group and the Hecke elements.** $\Gamma_t$ is a subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ whose elements are exactly those of [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37), the units which are local units of $R_1$ at every finite place other than $v$ (`hΓt`). For each $\ell$ there are $s_\ell\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ and a finite-idelic unit $sf_\ell$ with `hs`: $sf_\ell$ has component $s_\ell$ at every place not above $r$ and component $1$ at the places above $r$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\,\Lambda_1(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1)\,\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ is defined to be $\Gamma_t\cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ is given (`hwbar`).
--
--   **The special fibre and the formal module.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of dimension $2$ over the same ring with $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of $A_0$ in two variables, a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}\colon\Lambda\to \mathbb Z_{r^2}^{\,2}$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (additivity, normalisation at $1$, the Frobenius-twisted multiplication rule, injectivity, $r$-adic density and the trace identity), and `hA₀ : A₀.IsFormalModuleVia coord X₀ θ₀`, which says that $\theta_0$ is a system of formal coordinates for the group law of $A_0$ with underlying formal group $X_0$ and that the $\Lambda$-action is computed by $\mathrm{coord}$. Endomorphism families $e,e'$ of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma_t$, over the base (`he`), with degrees $\deg$.
--
--   **The endomorphism dictionary on the special fibre** (`hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4`, and the pair of order families `R₂`–`hE5g`, `Λ₁s`–`hE6f`; the clauses are summarised here). They assert: each $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure; $e$ is multiplicative and sends scalars in $\Gamma_t$ to multiplications, up to composing with multiplication by powers of $r$, and only scalars become multiplications; for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ to $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by a centraliser element whose matrix is $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)g^{-1}$; each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ carries $\Gamma_t$-labels in $\Lambda$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$; every level-preserving isogeny pair of $r$-power degree of a curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$; and there are $r$-integral orders $R_2\le R_1$ and $R_2'\le\Lambda_{1s}$ (with $\Lambda_{1s}$ a second maximal order such that $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_{1s}=R_1$, and $R_2\le R_2'$) carrying compatible actions $\hat e,\hat e'$ on $A_0$ which are additive on points, $\Lambda$-equivariant, level-preserving, unital, multiplicative, agree with the $\Lambda$-action on integers, satisfy the norm relation, extend one another, are star-stable and injective, match $e$ on $r$-power multiples of $\Gamma_t$, admit the same matrix dictionary, and satisfy the $q$-divisibility criterion `hE6f` for primes $q\neq r$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-side moduli package** (`ι`, `Φ`, `hΦ`, `hΦ4`, `MD`, `hMD`, `η`, `hη`, `E₀`, `hE₀`). A ring map $\iota\colon\mathbb Z_{r^2}\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ which is special for the reduction of $\iota$ and of height $4$, a moduli package $MD$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf, and a comparison map $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $MD$-points such that (`hη`, three clauses) on Noetherian bases $\eta$ identifies admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is compatible with base change along ring maps, and is locally surjective over a finite cover by localisations; together with an injective matrix dictionary $E_0$ for the centraliser of $\Phi$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the precise sense of `hE₀`.
--
--   **The formal uniformisation of the Drinfeld functor** (`eD`, `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD`). For Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a bijection, natural in $B$, between the $B$-points of $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\ \mathcal O\ MD$ and the pairs $(O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\Omega(B)$, where $\Omega$ is the functor of Deligne data for $(K_0,\pi)$; it preserves the first component, carries the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` to `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct`, sends $\pi$-translates to the Frobenius twist of the first component with the Deligne datum unchanged, and $\pi$-translates exist.
--
--   **Comparison of the two special fibres.** A ring map $\kappa$ from $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$ to $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), a natural number $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ exhibiting $\Phi$ and $\kappa_*X_0$ as isogenous of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`); a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$; and the Atkin–Lehner package at $\bar r$ on the special fibre: $A_{0w}$, morphisms $aw,aw',bw,bw'$ with the stated compatibilities, `hALw` (Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ realised by $aw,aw'$), `hBSw` (isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$), `hBSwlev` (level preservation) and `hJOINTw` (joint matrix dictionary matching $e\gamma$ with $\iota_0(\gamma)$ and $aw\ggg bw$ with $\iota_0(\bar w)$).
--
--   **The rigidification functor $\Xi$** (`hΞleg`, `hΞnat`, `hΞiso`, `hΞdef`). $\Xi$ assigns to each rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra a point of $\mathrm{GPoint}\ \mathcal O\ MD$; over connected bases its structure morphism is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$; it is compatible with pull-backs of rigidifications, invariant under isomorphisms of rigidified curves matching the rigidification data up to powers of $r$, and computed explicitly by `hΞdef` through a rigid transport with $j\le 1$ and $\eta$.
--
--   **The Hecke dictionary** (`g₀`, `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `heqS`). Over connected Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent bases, translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ corresponds, on $\Xi$-images, to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ for some $c\in\mathbb Z$; an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (with $\bar r$ invertible in the base) corresponds to $r^{c}g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$; and, for each $\ell$ and each datum $(n_1,s,sf,C_0,A_{0s},a_s,a_s',b_s,b_s')$ satisfying the Hecke and joint-dictionary hypotheses listed in `heqS`, a level-$\ell$ isogeny corresponds to $r^{c}g_0\iota_0(\ell s^{-1})g_0^{-1}$.
--
--   **The uniformisation of the fine level-$n$ moduli space** (`θt`, `Θf`, `hnat`, `hG`, `hi'`, `het`, `hfib`). A homomorphism $\theta_t\colon\Gamma_t\to G$ and a family $\Theta_f$ sending, for $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, triples $((\psi,P),g)$ to $B$-points of $M$ over $\mathcal O$, natural in $B$, equivariant for the right $G$-action via $\rho$, invariant under the twisted $\Gamma_t$-action composed with left translation by $\theta_t$, satisfying the unique infinitesimal lifting property `het` along surjections whose kernel has vanishing products, and satisfying the fibre criterion `hfib` over algebraically closed fields.
--
--   **The curve–datum correspondence** (`hC0e`, `hC0u`, `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p`, `hC2`, `hC2c`, `hC3`, `hC4`, `hC4pi`, `hC5`; the clauses are summarised here). They provide existence and essential uniqueness of the normalised level-$n$ transport of $P_0$; existence, uniqueness up to isomorphism of rigidified curves, and pull-back along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps of an "even" rigidified curve $(E,\varrho)$ whose $\Xi$-image has structure morphism the twist $\mathrm{Fr}^{-v(\det g_0)}\psi$ and corresponds to $(\psi,P)$ under $g_0^{-1}$; the identification of $\Theta_f((\psi,P),1)$ with the fine point of $(E,P_n)$ and, after composition with $p$, with the coarse point of $E$; the $\Gamma_t$-translation, $\mathrm{GL}_2$-action and $\pi$-translation compatibilities, including the effect on full level structures (twisting by $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$) and on extra level structures; and the one-leg clause `hC5`, which over an algebraically closed field compares two even rigidified curves with the same Deligne datum through an isomorphism and produces a matching $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$.
--
--   **The tower data on the special fibre** (`C₀`, `A₀s`, `as`, `as'`, `ks`, `bs`, `bs'`, `hLIs`, `hBSs`, `hBSslev`, `hJOINTs`, `hSTAB`, `hCLe`, `hCLu`). For each $\ell$ an extra level-$\ell$ structure $C_0(\ell)$ on $A_0$ together with the quotient curve $A_{0s}(\ell)$, the level-$\ell$ isogeny realising the quotient, a return isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_s(\ell)}$ preserving the level, and the joint matrix dictionary matching $e\gamma$ with $\iota_0(\gamma)$ and $a_s\ggg b_s$ with $\iota_0(\overline{s_\ell})$; the stabiliser identity `hSTAB`, which says that $e\gamma$ preserves $C_0(\ell)$ on points if and only if $\gamma\in\Gamma_{t,\ell}$; and `hCLe`, `hCLu`, the existence and uniqueness (as subfunctors of points) of an extra level-$\ell$ structure on $E$ transported through a rigidification from a given extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$, for $\ell\neq r$ invertible in the base.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a family $\Theta_c$ assigning to each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$, each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, and each pair $(\psi,P)$ consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ and a Deligne datum $P\in\Omega(B)$, a $B$-point of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\mathcal O$, that is, a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\mathcal Y_\ell$ whose composite with $g_\ell$ is the structure morphism of $\operatorname{Spec}B$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, such that the following two statements hold.
--
--   First, naturality: for every $\ell$, every two such bases $B$, $B'$ (Noetherian, with $\pi$ nilpotent and only trivial idempotents) and every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi\colon B\to B'$, and every $x\in(O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\Omega(B)$, the value $\Theta_c(\ell,B',\dots)$ at the image of $x$ under $\varphi$ equals the image of $\Theta_c(\ell,B,\dots)(x)$ under the functor $\mathrm{Scheme.nilpPoints}(g_\ell)$ applied to $\varphi$, i.e. the composite of $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ with that morphism.
--
--   Second, the characterisation on rigidified curves: for every $\ell$, every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent and only trivial idempotents, every $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B$, every $P\in\Omega(B)$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, every rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along the twist $\mathrm{Fr}^{-v(\det g_0)}\psi$, and every extra level-$\ell$ structure $C$ on $E$: if the structure morphism of $\Xi(B,\mathrm{Fr}^{-v(\det g_0)}\psi,\langle E,\varrho\rangle)$ is that same twist, if the pair $(\psi,P)$ is obtained from $\mathrm{eD}$ of that $\Xi$-value by the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$ (so that $\psi$ is the corresponding Frobenius twist of its first component and the lines of $P$ are the pull-backs of those of its Deligne datum along the action of $g_0$), and if $C$ is transported from $C_0(\ell)$ through $\varrho$ in the sense that for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t'\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}(B/\pi B)$ and every point $R$ of $\varrho.E_b$ over $t'$ whose composite with $\varrho.g_b$ factors through the closed immersion $C.\mathrm{levK}$, the composite of $R$ with $\varrho.\varphi$ and then $\varrho.g_A$ factors through $(C_0(\ell)).\mathrm{levK}$ — then the underlying morphism of $\Theta_c(\ell,B,\dots)(\psi,P)$ equals the underlying morphism of the coarse point $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ of the pair $\langle E,C\rangle$ over the structure morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$.
--
--   This is the step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation that propagates the $p$-adic uniformisation from the fine level-$n$ moduli space to the whole Hecke tower of coarse moduli schemes $\mathcal Y_\ell$ away from the two ramified primes, in the form of a family of $\mathcal Y_\ell$-valued points on Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent bases with connected spectrum, pinned down by its values on even rigidified curves with transported extra level structure. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_towerFamily_of_evenRigidifiedPair_of_heckeDictionary_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_oneLegC5`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_towerFamily_of_evenRigidifiedPair_of_heckeDictionary_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_oneLegC5).
